From 0d632814c97a5f84de7cd46b3fb46f5e2f316825 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:23:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] primitives: fill CTransaction's
 PrecomputedTransactionData lazily

Computing the sighash midstate at construction made every CTransaction
pay for three hashes over its inputs and outputs, including the many that
are never script-checked: blocks loaded during assumevalid IBD, blocks
read for reorgs or RPC, and transactions only relayed. Block
deserialization was about 70% slower than before the eager cache.

Keep the cache storage inline in CTransaction and fill it on the first
GetPrecomputedData() call. A one-byte atomic state (empty, writing,
ready) publishes it exactly once: the fast path is a single acquire load,
racing first callers each compute the deterministic result locally, and
only the caller that claims the slot writes it, so the fill neither
allocates nor races. The state byte uses existing tail padding, keeping
sizeof(CTransaction) at 352 bytes.

CTransaction is shared through CTransactionRef and is now explicitly
non-copyable. Only four tests copied one; they now construct or
deserialize straight into the reference.
